          "text": "A useful project scope does not start with a generic instruction to “recycle computers.” It starts with the firm’s confidentiality expectations. Those expectations should shape **vendor review, project scope, the records process, and the selected data-sanitization or physical-destruction method**. They should also set decision owners, escalation points, asset categories, acceptance criteria, evidence required, and final disposition routes."
